From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:50:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] egl: let a client trim the context current to its thread

EGL_MESA_context_trim adds eglTrimContextMESA(), found through
eglGetProcAddress.  A client that has flushed a context and left it idle calls
it to have the context release what it holds for completed work; the call
reaches pipe_context::trim through the DRI frontend and the state tracker.
Nothing current is nothing to trim, and a driver that cannot is an error
(EGL_BAD_ACCESS).

The state tracker first runs what glthread still has queued, so the objects it
was going to delete are no longer referenced when the driver looks, and then
asks the pipe context, which is the threaded context's driver thread when
there is one.  Nothing waits for the device.

The function takes no arguments, like eglWaitClient, and is not exported:
extension functions of the library are reached by name, and the GLVND lists
carry it so that the entrypoint check stays whole.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
